1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,840
 in this lecture will take a look at two AWS services

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,680
 for compliance and audit.

3
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:09,440
 So the first one is called as AWS artifact

4
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:12,540
 and AWS artifact provides on demand access

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:17,240
 to AWS compliance documentation and AWS agreement.

6
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:20,480
 So you can think of AWS artifact as a portal

7
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:23,960
 where all the compliance documentation

8
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:27,960
 related to AWS services is stored.

9
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:31,220
 So you can download AWS security and compliance documents

10
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:34,780
 such as ISO certification, PC IDSS, SOC report

11
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:37,280
 through either the console, AWS console,

12
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,720
 or if you are being evaluated by an auditor,

13
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:43,320
 you can create an IM role for the auditor

14
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:47,480
 through which he can go to this AWS artifact service

15
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:50,080
 and review the documentation.

16
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,840
 Okay, now let me just quickly show you

17
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,960
 through the console, AWS artifacts.

18
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:57,320
 Okay, IM on the AWS console.

19
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,940
 So let me just search for AWS artifacts.

20
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:06,000
 So I'm on the AWS artifact service

21
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,960
 and you can see here agreement reports and notification.

22
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,600
 So we just click on report

23
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:14,480
 and let's say I'm trying to be compliant with PC IDSS.

24
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:16,640
 So I can just search for PCI

25
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:21,680
 and you will see all the compliance reports from AWS

26
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:23,520
 are within this service.

27
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:27,680
 So you can see your PCI 3DS attestation compliance

28
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:31,640
 and then you can just go ahead and download these if required.

29
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:34,240
 Okay, so I think this pretty straightforward.

30
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:36,160
 Now let's go and take a look at the second service,

31
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:39,120
 which is AWS audit manager.

32
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:44,120
 So AWS audit manager continuously audit your AWS usage

33
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:47,760
 to assess risk and compliance with regulations

34
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,400
 and industry standards.

35
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:52,200
 So what AWS audit manager would do is

36
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,360
 so it will look at all the AWS services

37
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,280
 that you are using within the account

38
00:01:56,280 --> 00:02:00,200
 and then assess whether you are being compliant

39
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,720
 with the regulation in your industry.

40
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:06,320
 So it also provides some pre-built frameworks

41
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:08,880
 for well-known industry standards and regulations

42
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:12,640
 such as HIPAA, GDPR, PCI DSS and maps

43
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:17,040
 to customer AWS resources and SSS compliance.

44
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,360
 So now we can see the AWS audit manager

45
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:22,880
 is not just validating whether AWS services are compliant.

46
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,120
 It's looking at your usage of these services

47
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:29,160
 and whether they are compliant with the industry standard

48
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:32,480
 and regulations such as HIPAA, PCI DSS, et cetera.

49
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:35,040
 So how does it ensure you are compliant?

50
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:37,760
 It integrates and collects data

51
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:41,320
 from various AWS services such as cloud trail, security hub

52
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,760
 and others.

53
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:45,720
 And we'll take a look at cloud trail and some of these services

54
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,360
 but what it essentially does is

55
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:51,960
 it will take alerts from these different services

56
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:54,320
 and then map them to the pre-built frameworks

57
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:58,600
 for well-known industries and see if there's any deviation.

58
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:01,520
 And finally, AWS audit manager also assists

59
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:05,600
 in gathering and preparing evidence for audits.

60
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,160
 So rather than manually collecting evidence

61
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:12,440
 for your audits, it can help automate that process.

62
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:15,200
 Now let's just go to the console and just take a quick look.

63
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,760
 So let me just search for audit manager.

64
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:21,280
 And you can see AWS audit manager.

65
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:26,080
 Okay, now I am on the AWS audit manager.

66
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,760
 And now we can see on the left hand side,

67
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:30,040
 let me just click on assessments.

68
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:32,120
 And here you can see under assessments,

69
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:36,880
 access all your past and current assessments.

70
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:39,760
 You can select an assessment to review the evidence

71
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:42,120
 collected and generate assessment report.

72
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,720
 So we just click on create assessment

73
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:46,920
 and let me just give it a name demo.

74
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:51,560
 And then it shows where the final assessment should be sent.

75
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,200
 So you can provide a path for S3 bucket

76
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:56,520
 and then you have to select the framework.

77
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,720
 So you can see all the frameworks.

78
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:01,000
 Let me just click on this fedram

79
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,960
 and you can see here type standard

80
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:07,960
 and it has about 325 controls on which it evaluates your compliance.

81
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:11,440
 So let me just click on this.

82
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:14,240
 So on the left hand side, you can see access control

83
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:17,800
 that about 43 policies that you need to be compliant with.

84
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:20,920
 And on the right hand side, you can see the data sources.

85
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:25,360
 So if you want to be compliant with EC21,

86
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:28,840
 what the audit manager will do is it will gather data

87
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:33,160
 from AWS EPA calls your AWS cloud trail service,

88
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,320
 AWS config service, it'll be security hub service.

89
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:40,440
 And then map if you are being compliant.

90
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:44,680
 And in few cases like here being compliant with AC1,

91
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:48,360
 you have to gather the evidence manually.

92
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:52,720
 So hopefully it's clear to you how this audit manager works.

93
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,960
 So you can select the industry framework,

94
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:58,040
 then it is going to ingest the data from these different

95
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:02,760
 AWS services and then do the mapping and generate a report.

96
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:05,120
 So hopefully you are clear on the difference

97
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:09,200
 between AWS artifact and AWS audit manager

98
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:14,120
 because it's most likely going to be evaluated in the exam.

99
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,520
 I'll see you in the next lecture.

100
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,360
 Thank you.

